1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:05,588
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:12,470
[Arnaldo] <i>Do you know you're trespassing?</i>

3
00:00:12,554 --> 00:00:13,763
<i>This is private property.</i>

4
00:00:13,847 --> 00:00:16,975
<i>Mr. Mayor, my name is Ivy. Ivy Aguas.</i>

5
00:00:17,058 --> 00:00:18,601
[Ivy] <i>I've laid the trap.</i>

6
00:00:18,685 --> 00:00:21,896
<i>All we need is for him</i>
<i>to walk right into it.</i>

7
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:24,774
[Jepoy] <i>If we look at the status</i>
<i>of her assets,</i>

8
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:26,568
<i>she can be an investor here in Ardiente.</i>

9
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:27,527
<i>Good work.</i>

10
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:29,946
[Arnaldo] <i>You can have this</i>
<i>property, if you want.</i>

11
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:32,032
[Emilia] <i>I want that house!</i>
<i>That house is ours!</i>

12
00:00:32,115 --> 00:00:33,616
<i>That's mine! All mine!</i>

13
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,577
[Ivy] <i>What will it take, Mr. Mayor,</i>

14
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:38,163
<i>to make this property mine?</i>

15
00:00:38,246 --> 00:00:40,582
<i>Dinner at my place with the family.</i>

16
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:43,334
[Emilia] <i>Do you know I've been</i>
<i>eyeing that house?</i>

17
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:45,128
[Ivy] <i>What made you give it up, Governor?</i>

18
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:48,298
<i>Arnaldo convinced me to let you have it.</i>

19
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:50,341
[Ivy] <i>I admire people like you.</i>

20
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:53,052
<i>Those who know how to accept defeat.</i>

21
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:55,221
<i>But I never lose when it matters.</i>

22
00:00:55,305 --> 00:00:56,973
<i>Never? So, this was your first time?</i>

23
00:00:57,057 --> 00:00:58,183
[Julio] <i>I don't see any reason</i>

24
00:00:58,266 --> 00:01:00,477
<i>why you'd refuse my grandson's offer.</i>

25
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:03,521
<i>Of course, I still have to do my research.</i>

26
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:06,858
<i>And if everything looks fine,</i>
<i>I'll sign the agreement.</i>

27
00:01:06,941 --> 00:01:09,319
<i>Rare jewel… Very rare.</i>

28
00:01:09,402 --> 00:01:12,739
<i>But didn't you introduce me</i>
<i>to your brother the other day?</i>

29
00:01:12,822 --> 00:01:15,283
<i>Believe me, Ivy,</i>
<i>you're not missing anything.</i>

30
00:01:15,366 --> 00:01:17,452
[Julio] <i>In every family,</i>

31
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:19,662
<i>there always has to be</i>
<i>someone who's… weak.</i>

32
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:20,789
[Diego] <i>I've been thinking about this…</i>

33
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:23,708
<i>You look familiar. Have we met before?</i>

34
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:30,006
You think we've met before?

35
00:01:30,715 --> 00:01:34,761
[mellow piano music playing]

36
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:36,221
[clears throat]

37
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:39,808
Um… I don't think so.

38
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:44,938
I'm the type of woman you never forget…

39
00:01:46,105 --> 00:01:47,607
after you've met me.

40
00:01:49,734 --> 00:01:53,696
[mellow piano music continues]

41
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,284
Are you all right?

42
00:02:02,831 --> 00:02:04,249
I mean…

43
00:02:04,999 --> 00:02:07,710
I didn't think we'd wind up
in that conversation

44
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:11,422
when I asked the congressman about you.

45
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:14,717
Diego, I'm sorry--

46
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:16,261
You don't have to explain.

47
00:02:29,607 --> 00:02:31,025
[Ivy] Okay, sure. That'll work.

48
00:02:31,109 --> 00:02:34,154
Just email me the proposal
from Pandora Estates,

49
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:36,614
and I'll get back to you. Goodbye.

50
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:40,410
[tense music playing]

51
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:41,786
[sighs]

52
00:02:53,631 --> 00:02:54,591
[Emilia] <i>But I never lose</i>

53
00:02:54,674 --> 00:02:56,050
<i>when it matters.</i>

54
00:02:56,175 --> 00:02:58,094
<i>Never? So, this was your first time?</i>

55
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:06,978
Arnaldo took his guest home.

56
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:11,190
She's pretty, but too bad,

57
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:13,067
she doesn't look interested in you.

58
00:03:13,651 --> 00:03:15,945
Do you know anything about the export

59
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:18,239
processing zone Arnaldo mentioned?

60
00:03:18,364 --> 00:03:20,658
She probably thinks
you're too old for her.

61
00:03:22,827 --> 00:03:23,953
Listen, Raul…

62
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:25,872
I've stopped having people killed.

63
00:03:26,497 --> 00:03:30,376
[scoffs] Don't make me start
again. It's going to be messy

64
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:33,254
because it looks like Arnaldo
really likes her.

65
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:50,188
[pensive music playing]

66
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:04,369
I made a mistake, Nanny.

67
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:09,082
I shouldn't have said that to Emilia.

68
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:14,295
It'll only make it tougher
for me to gain her trust.

69
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:18,091
It's just so hard to hold back

70
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:20,301
when you're in front of the person…

71
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:25,723
who wronged you.
It's so hard to fight the anger.

72
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:31,938
How can I get what I want from
her if she doesn't trust me?

73
00:04:33,606 --> 00:04:36,359
Trust can't be rushed, sweetie.

74
00:04:38,778 --> 00:04:41,364
But I know ways to gain it.

75
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:49,038
[crickets chirping]

76
00:04:50,665 --> 00:04:52,583
Grandpa, you should get some rest.

77
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:54,210
[scoffs]

78
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:56,504
I like her.

79
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:59,007
You mean Ivy?

80
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:01,050
Mm-hm!

81
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,678
It was good judgment

82
00:05:03,761 --> 00:05:06,097
on your part to make her stay in Ardiente.

83
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:08,308
She's smart.

84
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:10,018
She's beautiful.

85
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:13,479
Financially independent.

86
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:18,318
Looks like my perception
of women is starting to change.

87
00:05:20,778 --> 00:05:22,071
You can use her.

88
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:25,116
That's all?

89
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:31,914
Every person we let into our
lives serves a purpose, Arnaldo.

90
00:05:33,291 --> 00:05:34,876
It's better that at this point,

91
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:37,420
you've already figured out
her purpose in your life.

92
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:42,383
It saves you the trouble of getting hurt.

93
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:44,844
It's a dirty business.

94
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:50,641
It makes you do things you
otherwise wouldn't want to do.

95
00:05:53,644 --> 00:05:56,814
Learn from your mother's mistakes.

96
00:06:02,028 --> 00:06:07,075
Oh, well. It's been quite a long day.

97
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:08,576
[breathes heavily]

98
00:06:08,826 --> 00:06:09,952
[groans]

99
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:13,790
[Julio] I will take your advice.

100
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:16,125
And get some rest.

101
00:06:16,834 --> 00:06:20,338
You should go to bed, too.
Good night, Arnaldo.

102
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:22,715
-All right, Grandpa.
-[Julio chuckles]

103
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:26,219
[Julio groans]

104
00:06:31,474 --> 00:06:36,979
[instrumental theme music playing]

105
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:56,582
[Ivy] <i>Are you all right?</i>

106
00:06:57,458 --> 00:06:59,669
<i>I didn't think we'd wind up</i>

107
00:06:59,752 --> 00:07:03,965
<i>in that conversation when I</i>
<i>asked the congressman about you.</i>

108
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:12,390
-[young Lily] <i>You're hurt.</i>
-[young Diego whimpering]

109
00:07:12,473 --> 00:07:16,602
<i>All right. Don't go</i>
<i>near the cliff again, okay?</i>

110
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:24,235
[instrumental theme music playing]

111
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:33,578
[Julio] <i>Looks like my perception</i>
<i>of women is starting to change.</i>

112
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:36,664
<i>You can use her.</i>

113
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:42,420
[Julio] <i>Every person we let into our lives</i>

114
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:44,380
<i>serves a purpose, Arnaldo.</i>

115
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:47,675
<i>It's better that at this point,</i>

116
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:49,802
<i>you've already figured</i>
<i>her purpose in your life.</i>

117
00:07:57,518 --> 00:08:01,022
[instrumental theme music playing]

118
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:21,375
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda plays]

119
00:08:47,568 --> 00:08:49,612
[song fades]

120
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:56,202
[sensual music playing]

121
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,511
Good morning. Time to get up.

122
00:09:18,182 --> 00:09:19,600
-Natalie.
-[Natalie chuckles softly]

123
00:09:19,892 --> 00:09:21,060
Good morning.

124
00:09:24,313 --> 00:09:26,148
Good morning. What are you doing here?

125
00:09:27,441 --> 00:09:28,693
Seriously?

126
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:32,405
Is that how you greet your future wife?

127
00:09:35,616 --> 00:09:36,742
S-sorry.

128
00:09:38,327 --> 00:09:40,538
[chuckles] Get up.

129
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:45,626
Daddy and your grandpa
are having breakfast right now.

130
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:48,546
And I'm sure they're talking
about the political marriage

131
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:50,047
of our families.

132
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:51,882
Are you excited?

133
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:57,680
-I'll just go take a shower.
-[Natalie chuckles]

134
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:01,934
Can I join you?

135
00:10:04,604 --> 00:10:06,272
-Sure.
-[chuckles]

136
00:10:16,449 --> 00:10:20,578
[tense music playing]

137
00:10:35,509 --> 00:10:40,139
[tense music continues playing]

138
00:11:12,671 --> 00:11:16,926
[tense music continues playing]

139
00:11:40,449 --> 00:11:42,451
[Pablo] Raul's not joining
us today, Julio?

140
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:48,624
Oh, I think he left quite early, Senator.

141
00:11:48,707 --> 00:11:49,834
Hmm.

142
00:11:50,042 --> 00:11:53,504
Well, you know, no rest
for the wicked, as they say.

143
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:54,338
[Pablo chuckles]

144
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:59,802
I'm sure he's just finalizing
everything for the campaign.

145
00:11:59,885 --> 00:12:01,220
[Pablo chuckles]

146
00:12:01,303 --> 00:12:02,888
I see you've finally realized

147
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:07,810
how much money is spent
on a national campaign.

148
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:15,359
It's nothing compared to what
we spend during local elections.

149
00:12:15,443 --> 00:12:16,402
[Pablo chuckles]

150
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:19,113
Well, we will get the funds.

151
00:12:21,782 --> 00:12:22,867
Right, Emilia?

152
00:12:23,993 --> 00:12:24,994
Of course, Papa.

153
00:12:25,077 --> 00:12:29,081
We're all here to help you
get to that Senate seat.

154
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:33,627
[Pablo] Of course. And you also
have our family's support.

155
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:37,506
After all, we're about to become family.

156
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:40,009
[Pablo and Julio chuckling]

157
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:42,011
[tense music playing]

158
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:43,971
[Pablo chuckles]

159
00:12:45,139 --> 00:12:46,891
In due time.

160
00:12:47,641 --> 00:12:51,520
Once Emilia's already
part of the Congress…

161
00:12:51,604 --> 00:12:52,480
[Pablo] Mm-hm.

162
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:56,233
And when Arnaldo runs for governor…

163
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:57,276
Oh.

164
00:12:57,818 --> 00:13:00,696
Everyone loves a royal wedding.

165
00:13:00,779 --> 00:13:02,323
[Pablo and Julio chuckle]

166
00:13:02,406 --> 00:13:03,824
[Pablo] You're right about that.

167
00:13:08,829 --> 00:13:09,914
[Pablo chuckles]

168
00:13:12,374 --> 00:13:14,793
[tense music playing]

169
00:13:25,638 --> 00:13:29,808
[tense music swells]

170
00:13:47,326 --> 00:13:48,327
[whistling]

171
00:13:48,994 --> 00:13:50,037
Hi, Auntie!

172
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:51,580
-Oh, you're here.
-[Raul chuckles]

173
00:13:51,705 --> 00:13:53,707
-Sorry. Did I surprise you?
-You're back so soon.

174
00:13:53,791 --> 00:13:55,751
I'm sorry I didn't give you a heads-up.

175
00:13:55,834 --> 00:13:57,336
Are you tired? Do you want to eat?

176
00:13:57,419 --> 00:13:59,672
-No, I'm fine.
-Let me set the table.

177
00:13:59,755 --> 00:14:03,467
I just want to rest a bit. You know why.

178
00:14:04,009 --> 00:14:08,514
I can hardly do what I want
in the place I'm staying at.

179
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:10,808
I could really use a breather.

180
00:14:11,183 --> 00:14:15,896
Then get some rest here.
I know you've had a long drive.

181
00:14:16,146 --> 00:14:19,733
I'll prepare breakfast for you.
She'll get up soon.

182
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:24,113
Don't worry about me.
Just continue doing your chores.

183
00:14:24,655 --> 00:14:28,117
I want to prepare
a meal for her. All by myself.

184
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:30,202
-Really? Are you sure?
-Yes.

185
00:14:30,286 --> 00:14:31,704
-That's sweet.
-[Raul chuckles]

186
00:14:31,787 --> 00:14:33,581
-I'll leave you then.
-Okay, Auntie.

187
00:14:33,664 --> 00:14:35,416
-I'll go out now.
-Okay.

188
00:14:35,499 --> 00:14:36,667
[caretaker] Okay.

189
00:14:42,464 --> 00:14:46,135
That's good to go.
Joan, I revised the memo.

190
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:48,888
Make sure everyone gets it, okay?

191
00:14:49,179 --> 00:14:50,639
And then update me, okay?

192
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:52,766
-Yes, Ms. Aguas.
-Thanks. You may go.

193
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:55,019
[sighs] Thank you, Nanny.

194
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:56,395
No problem.

195
00:14:57,396 --> 00:14:58,480
Here.

196
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:02,067
Um… Any news yet?

197
00:15:03,027 --> 00:15:04,695
I heard that

198
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:08,866
Governor Emilia has a meeting
regarding her foundation later.

199
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:12,286
Where at?

200
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,580
At her favorite restaurant.

201
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:18,792
[tense music playing]

202
00:15:22,171 --> 00:15:24,715
Then I'll start with
the first phase of the plan.

203
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:32,890
Starting today, I will befriend…

204
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:40,272
Governor Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.

205
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:44,318
[tense music swells]

206
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:06,131
Let's eat. I made you breakfast.

207
00:16:13,097 --> 00:16:14,223
[man 1] Hi, Governor.

208
00:16:14,306 --> 00:16:15,724
[man 2] Good morning, Governor.

209
00:16:15,975 --> 00:16:17,267
[woman] Good morning, ma'am.

210
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:24,274
[tense music playing]

211
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:39,415
-[Priscilla] Hi!
-Hi, ladies.

212
00:16:39,498 --> 00:16:40,582
Hi.

213
00:16:40,666 --> 00:16:41,458
[Emilia] Hello.

214
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:43,627
-[Christine] Hello
-[Emilia] Thank you for coming.

215
00:16:43,961 --> 00:16:44,837
[Emilia] Hi.

216
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,005
[Rica] Hello.

217
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:47,423
-Hello.
-[Christine] So, Emilia.

218
00:16:47,506 --> 00:16:50,426
Who's this woman we've been
seeing with the Mayor?

219
00:16:51,385 --> 00:16:53,804
[Christine] Your son has been
going around town with this

220
00:16:53,887 --> 00:16:55,431
unknown woman.

221
00:16:55,764 --> 00:16:57,141
Does Natalie know?

222
00:16:58,308 --> 00:16:59,935
She's just a friend.

223
00:17:00,269 --> 00:17:02,730
She's actually from
Manila. A family friend.

224
00:17:03,564 --> 00:17:08,861
[tense music swells]

225
00:17:13,949 --> 00:17:15,075
Ivy!

226
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:18,996
Hi, Governor.

227
00:17:19,496 --> 00:17:22,249
Oh, Ivy. What brings you here?

228
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:24,668
I might think you're stalking me.

229
00:17:25,627 --> 00:17:29,214
Uh… I'd be lying if I said I wasn't.

230
00:17:31,592 --> 00:17:33,135
So, why are you stalking me?

231
00:17:34,136 --> 00:17:36,930
Um, let's just say, to make it up to you.

232
00:17:37,973 --> 00:17:41,393
Because during the dinner last night…

233
00:17:41,894 --> 00:17:45,022
I felt that I may have taken
something you really wanted.

234
00:17:47,524 --> 00:17:49,234
Governor, I'm sorry, but…

235
00:17:50,152 --> 00:17:52,821
I just really wanted that property.

236
00:17:53,781 --> 00:17:58,827
So I thought maybe there's some
way I can make it up to you.

237
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:04,500
Maybe I can help in your foundation.

238
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:10,339
Of course, dear. Who am I to refuse those

239
00:18:10,422 --> 00:18:13,842
who wish to support the Ardiente
Women's Association?

240
00:18:14,384 --> 00:18:15,385
Come join us.

241
00:18:15,886 --> 00:18:18,639
Ladies, I'd like you
to meet Ms. Ivy Aguas.

242
00:18:18,889 --> 00:18:21,391
She's the president
and owner of Aguas Realty.

243
00:18:21,809 --> 00:18:23,018
Come, Ivy, join us.

244
00:18:23,185 --> 00:18:24,937
Christine, do you mind
moving one seat, please?

245
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:26,480
-Sure.
-I'd like to sit beside her.

246
00:18:26,563 --> 00:18:27,648
-[Christine] Okay.
-Come, Ivy.

247
00:18:27,731 --> 00:18:28,816
Thank you, Governor.

248
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:31,944
Ivy, I'd like you to meet Christine…

249
00:18:32,069 --> 00:18:33,529
-Hi, Christine.
-Vicky…

250
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:34,488
-Hi.
-Nice to meet you.

251
00:18:34,571 --> 00:18:36,532
-Rica and Priscilla.
-Hello, I'm Ivy.

252
00:18:36,615 --> 00:18:37,950
[Emilia] This is Ms. Aguas.

253
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:39,660
Ivy. Ivy Aguas.

254
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:45,415
So, Governor,
how can I help your foundation?

255
00:18:45,499 --> 00:18:48,335
Do you have any new programs?

256
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:50,838
We have a lot of programs, Ms. Ivy.

257
00:18:50,921 --> 00:18:52,089
-Yes.
-In fact,

258
00:18:52,172 --> 00:18:53,674
we're launching a mass feeding,

259
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:55,801
and then we have a medical mission

260
00:18:55,884 --> 00:18:58,971
for the senior citizens, and…
What else do we have?

261
00:18:59,263 --> 00:19:01,390
I think we have a benefit concert, right?

262
00:19:01,473 --> 00:19:02,683
-[Christine] Yeah.
-[Emilia] Yeah.

263
00:19:02,891 --> 00:19:04,393
-[Christine] Soon.
-Mm-hm.

264
00:19:04,476 --> 00:19:06,687
Can I come, too?

265
00:19:06,770 --> 00:19:10,190
Of course, Ivy!
We'd love to have you there!

266
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:11,608
-[Christine] Yes, yeah.
-Thank you.

267
00:19:11,692 --> 00:19:15,154
It's so nice of you, Ivy. Have some tea.

268
00:19:15,237 --> 00:19:16,155
Okay.

269
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:17,239
[Christine] This one.

270
00:19:17,906 --> 00:19:19,908
-[Ivy] Thank you.
-[Priscilla] Okay.

271
00:19:20,617 --> 00:19:22,911
[tense music swells]

272
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:24,746
Thank you.

273
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:38,760
[Arnaldo] Uh…
I'm going to the municipal hall

274
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:40,679
to sign some papers, and then…

275
00:19:41,221 --> 00:19:43,348
That's it. After that, I'm free.

276
00:19:43,807 --> 00:19:44,808
Awww.

277
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:47,311
-I'll miss you.
-I'll miss you, too.

278
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:50,230
I'll be with dad in his office…

279
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:51,190
Mm-hm.

280
00:19:51,273 --> 00:19:55,277
…in San Isidro. I'll be back, okay?

281
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:56,820
Yeah. See you later.

282
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:16,340
-[cans jangling]
-[suspenseful music playing]

283
00:20:27,684 --> 00:20:28,435
[door closes]

284
00:20:34,858 --> 00:20:36,902
[jangling]

285
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:40,489
[melancholic music playing]

286
00:20:41,073 --> 00:20:41,949
[Pablo] <i>That's Arthur.</i>

287
00:20:42,032 --> 00:20:44,910
<i>He's the key to the zero crime rate.</i>

288
00:20:45,285 --> 00:20:47,287
[Arthur] <i>That's not true!</i>
<i>This place is pure evil!</i>

289
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:49,748
<i>There'll come a day</i>
<i>this town will cease to exist.</i>

290
00:20:53,043 --> 00:20:54,044
[exhales]

291
00:20:57,005 --> 00:20:58,006
[exhales]

292
00:21:02,135 --> 00:21:05,347
[Arthur] <i>Jessica Vergara?</i>
<i>What is it, murder or rape?</i>

293
00:21:05,430 --> 00:21:07,641
[Dante] <i>Both. She went missing,</i>
<i>was found floating</i>

294
00:21:07,724 --> 00:21:10,894
<i>in a river a week later.</i>
<i>Before that, she allegedly</i>

295
00:21:10,978 --> 00:21:12,854
<i>had an affair with Raul Torillo.</i>

296
00:21:14,856 --> 00:21:16,775
This town will cease to exist.

297
00:21:19,361 --> 00:21:24,783
At the right time, the whole
Ardiente family will be gone.

298
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:27,494
[suspenseful music playing]

299
00:21:27,577 --> 00:21:28,578
[chuckles]

300
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:52,227
Mmm.

301
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:53,353
Not too much, okay?

302
00:21:53,603 --> 00:21:58,025
There's a feeding program later.
We might only have a few buyers.

303
00:21:58,108 --> 00:21:59,526
They might even ask for store credit.

304
00:22:01,778 --> 00:22:07,326
I guess Ms. Ivy's one
of the governor's friends now.

305
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:09,703
What?

306
00:22:09,786 --> 00:22:14,875
[Filipino folk music playing]

307
00:22:17,961 --> 00:22:20,756
[Loring] <i>She's now one of</i>
<i>your mother's angels</i>

308
00:22:20,839 --> 00:22:22,299
<i>at the foundation.</i>

309
00:22:23,383 --> 00:22:28,680
[Loring] I liked her at first,
but now I don't know

310
00:22:28,764 --> 00:22:32,184
what to think of her. She's been rubbing

311
00:22:32,267 --> 00:22:34,478
elbows with your brother and mother.

312
00:22:34,686 --> 00:22:37,606
-[Filipino folk music playing]
-[clapping]

313
00:22:43,111 --> 00:22:46,031
[Loring] <i>I must've had</i>
<i>the wrong impression of her.</i>

314
00:22:47,908 --> 00:22:51,620
You make it sound like
Arnaldo and Mom are evil.

315
00:22:52,329 --> 00:22:53,330
Oh.

316
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:57,459
I'm sorry, dear.
I didn't mean it that way.

317
00:22:57,793 --> 00:23:01,671
I know you love them. They're your family.

318
00:23:02,172 --> 00:23:04,883
[Filipino folk music playing]

319
00:23:04,966 --> 00:23:08,220
[clapping]

320
00:23:11,807 --> 00:23:13,558
[no audible dialogue]

321
00:23:13,683 --> 00:23:15,143
[Loring] Anyway, who cares if

322
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:18,188
Ms. Ivy gets close to them, right?

323
00:23:18,271 --> 00:23:21,441
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

324
00:23:21,650 --> 00:23:24,903
I'm sorry, just ignore
what I'm saying. Don't mind me.

325
00:23:26,863 --> 00:23:30,408
[Filipino folk music playing]

326
00:23:36,373 --> 00:23:39,960
[applause]

327
00:23:43,505 --> 00:23:46,675
[clapping and cheering]

328
00:23:51,429 --> 00:23:54,850
[emcee] There you go.
Thank you, performers.

329
00:23:55,058 --> 00:23:57,811
Now I'm honored to call to the podium,

330
00:23:58,145 --> 00:24:02,274
our beloved governor,
Gov. Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.

331
00:24:02,399 --> 00:24:05,610
[crowd clapping and cheering]

332
00:24:09,781 --> 00:24:12,242
[no audible dialogue]

333
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:23,712
Hello, friends!

334
00:24:23,795 --> 00:24:25,672
[clapping and cheering]

335
00:24:25,755 --> 00:24:27,924
Take your seats!

336
00:24:28,258 --> 00:24:30,886
You can sit down now. Please, sit.

337
00:24:31,678 --> 00:24:34,723
[Emilia] This has been
our annual activity, right?

338
00:24:34,848 --> 00:24:37,267
But this year, it's more special.

339
00:24:37,517 --> 00:24:40,395
My friends have also visited to help.

340
00:24:40,687 --> 00:24:43,773
Let's give them a hand.
Stand up. Come on, friends.

341
00:24:44,691 --> 00:24:47,861
[Emilia] These ladies help me out here

342
00:24:47,944 --> 00:24:51,281
in the Ardiente Women's Association.

343
00:24:51,364 --> 00:24:52,157
All right.

344
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:56,453
This year, we've been blessed
with another sister!

345
00:24:56,620 --> 00:25:01,708
Our newest, dearest friend, Ivy Aguas!

346
00:25:04,586 --> 00:25:05,837
Thank you, Governor.

347
00:25:05,921 --> 00:25:07,631
Thank <i>you</i>!

348
00:25:07,756 --> 00:25:10,300
[clapping continues]

349
00:25:10,592 --> 00:25:11,593
Hello.

350
00:25:18,975 --> 00:25:20,602
[Emilia] Enjoy your food.

351
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:21,686
There's more than enough for everyone.

352
00:25:21,770 --> 00:25:24,064
You can get more food at the table.

353
00:25:24,147 --> 00:25:25,398
[woman coughing]

354
00:25:25,482 --> 00:25:29,069
Ma'am? Have some water.

355
00:25:30,320 --> 00:25:32,656
Letty? Letty! Come here.

356
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:36,243
She needs help. Come here. Assist her.

357
00:25:38,662 --> 00:25:40,121
[Emilia] Enjoy your food.

358
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:41,790
How are you doing?

359
00:25:42,540 --> 00:25:43,792
-Is everything good?
-They're okay.

360
00:25:43,875 --> 00:25:44,918
[Emilia] How about you?

361
00:25:45,001 --> 00:25:46,461
Ma'am, enjoy your meal, okay?

362
00:25:46,544 --> 00:25:47,420
Excuse me.

363
00:25:50,006 --> 00:25:51,174
Excuse me. Is everything okay here?

364
00:25:51,258 --> 00:25:53,426
Yeah, I got sponsors for next year.

365
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:54,344
That's good.

366
00:25:54,427 --> 00:25:56,763
They'll donate canned goods.

367
00:25:56,846 --> 00:25:59,849
-Oh, yeah? That's good to know.
-[Christine] Yeah.

368
00:26:02,686 --> 00:26:03,687
[Emilia] And then?

369
00:26:07,148 --> 00:26:08,566
[Emilia] Is everything okay?

370
00:26:08,692 --> 00:26:11,069
-[Christine] Yeah.
-Everyone all right?

371
00:26:11,278 --> 00:26:13,071
[Ivy] Eat slowly now.

372
00:26:14,531 --> 00:26:15,949
Is she okay?

373
00:26:16,032 --> 00:26:18,201
-Yes.
-Let me help.

374
00:26:19,452 --> 00:26:22,706
Ma'am, you're coughing. Have some water.

375
00:26:22,789 --> 00:26:24,791
[woman] Thank you, Ma'am. Thank you.

376
00:26:24,874 --> 00:26:26,418
-[Ivy] All right.
-[woman] Thank you.

377
00:26:26,501 --> 00:26:29,671
Take this. It's mine.

378
00:26:30,005 --> 00:26:31,256
-[Ivy] Here.
-Thank you.

379
00:26:31,339 --> 00:26:33,425
You can use it to cover your mouth.

380
00:26:33,508 --> 00:26:37,053
We have to cut these into smaller pieces.

381
00:26:37,345 --> 00:26:38,888
That must be why you're coughing.

382
00:26:38,972 --> 00:26:41,474
-[woman] Thank you.
-Here, so you can eat better.

383
00:26:41,558 --> 00:26:42,726
Thank you, ma'am.

384
00:26:42,809 --> 00:26:45,603
[Ivy] No problem. There you go, ma'am.

385
00:26:45,812 --> 00:26:47,230
-You're all set.
-Thank you.

386
00:26:47,314 --> 00:26:50,650
May I join this group, Ms. Ivy?

387
00:26:52,694 --> 00:26:53,945
Mr. Mayor.

388
00:26:54,029 --> 00:26:57,741
-[crowd grows excited]
-Good day. Good day, everyone.

389
00:26:57,824 --> 00:26:58,825
[man 1] Hi, Mayor.

390
00:26:59,701 --> 00:27:02,871
[Arnaldo chuckles] Good day.
Good day, everyone.

391
00:27:02,954 --> 00:27:03,955
[man 2] Hi, Mayor.

392
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:05,206
[Arnaldo] Good day.

393
00:27:05,915 --> 00:27:07,250
[Ivy] Eat well.

394
00:27:07,334 --> 00:27:08,335
Good day.

395
00:27:10,837 --> 00:27:14,049
[tense music playing]

396
00:27:14,883 --> 00:27:16,092
[Natalie] Yes, Auntie?

397
00:27:16,593 --> 00:27:18,845
I just got back from San Isidro.

398
00:27:20,013 --> 00:27:21,222
[chuckles]

399
00:27:21,306 --> 00:27:23,725
Okay, I guess I'll join you then.

400
00:27:25,435 --> 00:27:28,355
All right. I'll see you later,
Auntie Emilia.

401
00:27:28,855 --> 00:27:31,483
I'm so excited. Bye.

402
00:27:38,698 --> 00:27:41,576
[Arnaldo] Go on.
Please take all these gifts home

403
00:27:41,659 --> 00:27:43,370
with you to your families.

404
00:27:43,578 --> 00:27:46,956
-[Ivy] Go on.
-Have some more! Don't be shy!

405
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:50,085
This is for you, ma'am.

406
00:27:50,251 --> 00:27:51,503
Of course, I'll give you one, too.

407
00:27:51,586 --> 00:27:53,421
-[woman 1] Thank you.
-[woman 2] Thank you.

408
00:27:53,505 --> 00:27:54,672
[Ivy] We still have more.

409
00:27:54,756 --> 00:27:56,424
Give them some more.

410
00:27:57,008 --> 00:27:59,427
-These are for you.
-[man] Thank you.

411
00:28:01,304 --> 00:28:03,640
-Did you have a good time?
-[Arnaldo clears throat]

412
00:28:06,893 --> 00:28:07,977
[Ivy] Oh.

413
00:28:08,853 --> 00:28:11,523
No, thank you, Mr. Mayor. I'm fine.

414
00:28:11,606 --> 00:28:14,401
I insist. I know you gave your hanky away.

415
00:28:16,027 --> 00:28:18,238
Mr. Mayor, it's okay. Thank you.

416
00:28:21,658 --> 00:28:22,742
[Natalie] Arnaldo!

417
00:28:23,952 --> 00:28:25,495
[chuckles] Babe!

418
00:28:26,955 --> 00:28:27,956
[smooches]

419
00:28:28,331 --> 00:28:29,332
Hi, Auntie!

420
00:28:30,166 --> 00:28:32,710
[Natalie] Your mom called me,
and she invited me here.

421
00:28:33,378 --> 00:28:34,879
She told me to join you.

422
00:28:36,464 --> 00:28:38,216
So, who's your new friend?

423
00:28:39,801 --> 00:28:40,969
[Arnaldo] Uh…

424
00:28:41,052 --> 00:28:42,804
Uh… Ivy Aguas.

425
00:28:43,054 --> 00:28:44,764
[tense music playing]

426
00:28:44,889 --> 00:28:45,932
Natalie.

427
00:28:47,684 --> 00:28:49,269
I'm Arnaldo's girlfriend.

428
00:28:49,853 --> 00:28:50,645
Mmm.

429
00:28:50,729 --> 00:28:52,147
-[Ivy] Nice to meet you.
-[Natalie] You, too.

430
00:28:52,230 --> 00:28:54,566
-I'm Ivy Aguas
-Hello.

431
00:28:54,649 --> 00:28:59,904
I'm actually new here.
That's why we haven't met.

432
00:29:00,447 --> 00:29:02,198
[Natalie] Well, how do you find it so far?

433
00:29:02,282 --> 00:29:05,034
Have you been enjoying
yourself here in Ardiente?

434
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:06,494
I love it here, Natalie.

435
00:29:06,578 --> 00:29:08,496
-[Ivy] Really.
-[Natalie chuckles]

436
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:12,208
I'm actually considering
staying for a while.

437
00:29:12,292 --> 00:29:14,127
[Natalie chuckling] Oh!

438
00:29:14,294 --> 00:29:16,463
So, you plan on staying.

439
00:29:17,630 --> 00:29:18,506
Yes.

440
00:29:18,590 --> 00:29:19,549
[Natalie chuckling] Oh, great.

441
00:29:21,342 --> 00:29:22,802
Well, excuse me.

442
00:29:22,886 --> 00:29:23,928
Okay.

443
00:29:26,264 --> 00:29:28,057
-Babe, I missed you!
-Friends!

444
00:29:28,141 --> 00:29:29,225
Our work is done, everyone.

445
00:29:29,309 --> 00:29:30,560
-[Natalie] Let's go!
-[Arnaldo] Okay.

446
00:29:30,977 --> 00:29:33,271
-[Natalie] Hello!
-[Emilia] Thank you, everyone.

447
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:56,795
Don't you know how to pass a ball?!

448
00:29:56,878 --> 00:29:58,338
[kid 2] It's because you're fat!

449
00:29:58,421 --> 00:30:00,590
[kid 3] And he's clumsy, too.

450
00:30:00,840 --> 00:30:06,221
[kids] Piggy! Piggy!

451
00:30:06,304 --> 00:30:08,681
Hey. That's enough.

452
00:30:09,599 --> 00:30:11,851
You shouldn't do that.

453
00:30:12,185 --> 00:30:13,311
You're hurting his feelings.

454
00:30:13,728 --> 00:30:15,063
-Sorry.
-Sorry.

455
00:30:15,814 --> 00:30:18,149
-Let's go.
-Go on home.

456
00:30:21,945 --> 00:30:25,698
[somber piano music playing]

457
00:30:34,707 --> 00:30:35,792
What's your name?

458
00:30:35,875 --> 00:30:36,835
Leo, sir.

459
00:30:40,296 --> 00:30:43,049
Leo… I'm Diego.

460
00:30:43,967 --> 00:30:47,345
Do you live here?
I haven't seen you before.

461
00:30:47,595 --> 00:30:50,306
I'm just visiting my grandma.

462
00:30:55,228 --> 00:30:57,146
Don't let those bullies get to you.

463
00:30:57,730 --> 00:31:00,859
Even if they call you names,
don't listen to them.

464
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:06,447
Always remember, you know
yourself better than anyone.

465
00:31:07,115 --> 00:31:08,283
Thank you.

466
00:31:09,617 --> 00:31:12,579
I think I should go home now.

467
00:31:14,247 --> 00:31:15,707
Okay, take care.

468
00:31:22,589 --> 00:31:23,965
[Lily] <i>I'll teach you how to lose weight</i>

469
00:31:24,048 --> 00:31:25,675
<i>while still enjoying food.</i>

470
00:31:25,758 --> 00:31:27,176
<i>See, you did it!</i>

471
00:31:27,260 --> 00:31:31,806
<i>It was hard, but you made it!</i>
<i>Just tell yourself you can!</i>

472
00:31:32,515 --> 00:31:37,937
[pensive music playing]

473
00:31:49,490 --> 00:31:50,533
[Julio] Your mother…

474
00:31:50,909 --> 00:31:51,910
[grunts]

475
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:55,955
She loves to make decisions she thinks

476
00:31:56,039 --> 00:31:57,832
is best for everyone.

477
00:31:58,625 --> 00:32:00,627
But the truth is, they aren't.

478
00:32:01,169 --> 00:32:07,342
That's why if it's not too
much damage, just let it slide.

479
00:32:08,176 --> 00:32:09,177
After all…

480
00:32:10,470 --> 00:32:12,680
Ivy's investment is in the works, right?

481
00:32:13,806 --> 00:32:14,807
Yes, Grandpa.

482
00:32:16,476 --> 00:32:19,020
Oh. Tell me, Arnaldo.

483
00:32:21,439 --> 00:32:27,195
How did Natalie handle meeting Ivy?

484
00:32:27,904 --> 00:32:31,074
-She got possessive.
-[Julio laughs]

485
00:32:32,951 --> 00:32:35,912
I had that feeling, I did.

486
00:32:39,290 --> 00:32:43,127
Is it hard to be so handsome, grandson?

487
00:32:45,505 --> 00:32:46,631
Well…

488
00:32:47,215 --> 00:32:54,180
What you shouldn't forget
is that Natalie is your future.

489
00:32:56,140 --> 00:32:59,936
Actually, Natalie is
the future of this family.

490
00:33:00,561 --> 00:33:05,566
We can't afford to lose them from our side

491
00:33:05,650 --> 00:33:09,862
because we need them
at the national stage.

492
00:33:10,530 --> 00:33:11,572
And Ivy…

493
00:33:12,448 --> 00:33:13,700
[Julio chuckles] Ivy…

494
00:33:15,284 --> 00:33:20,206
She's nice to have, but on the side.

495
00:33:21,040 --> 00:33:23,710
It's like eating steak.

496
00:33:24,043 --> 00:33:26,379
We have a lot of side dishes,

497
00:33:26,796 --> 00:33:30,049
but never exchange prime beef…

498
00:33:31,884 --> 00:33:33,803
for a measly side dish.

499
00:33:34,137 --> 00:33:35,138
Remember that.

500
00:33:38,850 --> 00:33:39,851
Cheers?

501
00:33:42,770 --> 00:33:43,688
[glasses clink]

502
00:33:43,771 --> 00:33:44,772
You're good.

503
00:33:50,778 --> 00:33:53,114
[Carlotta] It's time to eat, sweetie.

504
00:33:58,745 --> 00:34:00,288
The Ardientes are unbelievable.

505
00:34:02,290 --> 00:34:07,795
They're so good at manipulating
people, especially Emilia.

506
00:34:08,546 --> 00:34:12,175
She's only gotten worse.
She's rotten to the core.

507
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:14,802
[sighs]

508
00:34:15,011 --> 00:34:19,265
I'm finding out so many
new things about the Ardientes.

509
00:34:20,683 --> 00:34:22,685
But I still don't have any evidence…

510
00:34:23,644 --> 00:34:25,772
that could link them
to my mother's murder.

511
00:34:26,147 --> 00:34:29,859
Sweetie… You're looking
for justice, right?

512
00:34:30,276 --> 00:34:33,071
It'll take you a while
before you find evidence.

513
00:34:33,404 --> 00:34:37,533
But if you're after revenge,
it's as quick as one bullet.

514
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:39,118
Sweetie?

515
00:34:39,702 --> 00:34:43,539
[tense music swelling]

516
00:34:51,923 --> 00:34:52,965
[suspenseful sting]

517
00:34:58,596 --> 00:34:59,847
[line ringing]

518
00:34:59,972 --> 00:35:00,973
Hello?

519
00:35:02,725 --> 00:35:04,435
I have a job for you.

520
00:35:08,397 --> 00:35:09,690
[Emilia] Ivy, thank you so much

521
00:35:09,774 --> 00:35:12,568
for joining us
at our foundation's fundraiser.

522
00:35:13,111 --> 00:35:15,196
I really enjoyed myself, Governor.

523
00:35:15,279 --> 00:35:18,574
I got to know more around Ardiente.

524
00:35:20,326 --> 00:35:22,370
Hey, I'm sorry about Natalie.

525
00:35:22,453 --> 00:35:26,749
Arnaldo didn't tell me
he hadn't introduced her to you.

526
00:35:27,250 --> 00:35:28,501
I'm sorry about that.

527
00:35:29,752 --> 00:35:33,047
Governor, you don't need to apologize.

528
00:35:33,756 --> 00:35:37,093
Actually, I really feel
Natalie and I will get along.

529
00:35:38,261 --> 00:35:39,428
That's good to know!

530
00:35:39,512 --> 00:35:42,014
I invited them for coffee.
Want to join us?

531
00:35:42,306 --> 00:35:44,267
I don't have plans, so sure.
I'll see you--

532
00:35:44,350 --> 00:35:47,395
Okay, wait. I'll have
one of my guards drive your car.

533
00:35:47,478 --> 00:35:49,397
-Okay, sure.
-[Emilia] Drive her car, okay?

534
00:35:49,480 --> 00:35:51,858
-[body guard] Yes, ma'am.
-Follow us there. Let's go!

535
00:35:51,941 --> 00:35:52,942
Yeah.

536
00:35:58,573 --> 00:35:59,782
[Emilia] Ivy, let's go.

537
00:36:01,284 --> 00:36:02,285
[car door closes]

538
00:36:02,743 --> 00:36:04,787
By the way, looks like Arnaldo is here.

539
00:36:04,871 --> 00:36:06,289
The guard dog is here!

540
00:36:06,372 --> 00:36:08,082
Come, join me.

541
00:36:10,251 --> 00:36:11,210
[Emilia] Is Arnaldo here?

542
00:36:11,294 --> 00:36:12,295
[no audible dialogue]

543
00:36:12,378 --> 00:36:14,505
[Emilia] Good. Come on, Ivy.

544
00:36:15,840 --> 00:36:17,216
Emilia Ardiente-Torillo!

545
00:36:17,383 --> 00:36:20,720
[tense music plays]

546
00:36:25,391 --> 00:36:26,767
Your days are over!

547
00:36:27,143 --> 00:36:28,311
-Governor!
-Gov! Gov!

548
00:36:28,436 --> 00:36:30,438
-[gunfire]
-[screams]

549
00:36:30,563 --> 00:36:34,400
[tense music swells]

550
00:36:36,611 --> 00:36:37,695
Help her!

551
00:36:37,778 --> 00:36:40,489
[gasps] Ivy! Ivy!

552
00:36:40,573 --> 00:36:41,574
[Jepoy] Move!

553
00:36:46,579 --> 00:36:48,581
-Stop!
-[gunshot]

554
00:36:48,915 --> 00:36:52,793
[action music plays]

555
00:36:53,336 --> 00:36:54,879
[Arnaldo] What happened?!

556
00:36:54,962 --> 00:36:56,756
[Emilia] Hello? Hello, doc?

557
00:36:56,839 --> 00:36:59,425
There's an emergency! Yes, at home!

558
00:37:01,761 --> 00:37:03,179
[Jepoy] Get up! You bastard.

559
00:37:03,804 --> 00:37:05,765
[grunts]

560
00:37:07,808 --> 00:37:08,559
Start the car, hurry!

561
00:37:08,643 --> 00:37:11,938
[Emilia] We have an emergency!
Oh, no, Ivy! Faster!

562
00:37:12,021 --> 00:37:12,980
Arnaldo.

563
00:37:16,525 --> 00:37:17,526
Arnaldo!

564
00:37:22,907 --> 00:37:24,951
-[action music playing]
-[grunts]

565
00:37:25,201 --> 00:37:26,202
Get up.

566
00:37:37,630 --> 00:37:38,589
[man] Shoot him!

567
00:37:51,519 --> 00:37:54,605
[Emilia] Ivy? Ivy, just hang in there.

568
00:37:54,981 --> 00:37:58,609
Wait, I have to call Raul. Hurry! Faster!

569
00:37:58,693 --> 00:38:00,361
-Fernandez!
-Sir?

570
00:38:00,695 --> 00:38:01,445
What happened?

571
00:38:01,529 --> 00:38:03,239
Sir, someone was after Governor.

572
00:38:03,406 --> 00:38:04,699
But Ivy got shot.

573
00:38:04,824 --> 00:38:05,950
What?

574
00:38:10,788 --> 00:38:12,081
[Arnaldo] Hurry.

575
00:38:12,498 --> 00:38:15,418
-[Ivy] Hospital…
-[Arnaldo] No, you're fine here.

576
00:38:16,419 --> 00:38:18,004
[Dr. Hizon] Mayor, we'll take care of her.

577
00:38:23,634 --> 00:38:26,512
Sir. I'm sorry, but you can't enter.

578
00:38:28,180 --> 00:38:29,348
Is that right?

579
00:38:30,016 --> 00:38:34,979
[tense music playing]

580
00:38:36,939 --> 00:38:38,065
Are you okay?

581
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:39,442
[Emilia] Um…

582
00:38:39,775 --> 00:38:43,362
She saved me. She saved my life.

583
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:46,240
[Dr. Hizon] Please clear the
area. We need space.

584
00:38:47,950 --> 00:38:49,285
[Ivy groans]

585
00:38:50,786 --> 00:38:53,247
[groaning]

586
00:38:53,914 --> 00:38:58,753
[tense music swells]

587
00:39:11,515 --> 00:39:13,059
Have you spoken to your father?

588
00:39:13,309 --> 00:39:16,771
He hasn't been
answering my calls. Where is he?

589
00:39:16,854 --> 00:39:17,855
You know him, Mom.

590
00:39:20,066 --> 00:39:22,318
Doc? How's Ivy?

591
00:39:22,735 --> 00:39:24,236
The wound isn't serious.

592
00:39:24,487 --> 00:39:25,863
There's nothing to worry about.

593
00:39:26,864 --> 00:39:28,032
You're gonna be okay.

594
00:39:28,783 --> 00:39:29,784
Papa.

595
00:39:32,203 --> 00:39:34,246
[Dr. Hizon] The painkillers
will keep you sedated.

596
00:39:34,455 --> 00:39:37,792
But you need some rest.
I'll be on my way now.

597
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,126
Mayor, Governor.

598
00:39:39,794 --> 00:39:40,836
[Emilia] Thank you, doc.

599
00:39:47,259 --> 00:39:49,053
Stay with Ivy, Arnaldo.

600
00:39:49,845 --> 00:39:51,389
I'll take care of everything.

601
00:39:53,224 --> 00:39:57,019
[footsteps receding]

602
00:39:58,604 --> 00:40:02,483
[tense music playing]

603
00:40:05,778 --> 00:40:06,779
[door closes]

604
00:40:11,867 --> 00:40:15,246
Idiots! You worthless guards!

605
00:40:15,371 --> 00:40:16,747
[Emilia] Papa, that's enough.

606
00:40:16,831 --> 00:40:20,126
Don't worry. I didn't get shot. I'm fine.

607
00:40:20,209 --> 00:40:22,670
Shut up! I don't care about that!

608
00:40:22,753 --> 00:40:24,171
That is not the point!

609
00:40:24,463 --> 00:40:27,758
The point is someone dared
to go against me!

610
00:40:28,134 --> 00:40:33,264
And I am the pillar of Ardiente!
No one must know about this.

611
00:40:34,181 --> 00:40:37,560
The people will think I'm weak
if word of this gets out.

612
00:40:38,185 --> 00:40:43,983
This will affect my candidacy.
Have you thought about that?!

613
00:40:45,109 --> 00:40:47,027
You stupid men!

614
00:40:47,820 --> 00:40:50,197
[panting]

615
00:40:52,908 --> 00:40:54,743
Why didn't you take me to the hospital?

616
00:40:56,829 --> 00:40:58,998
We have to be careful
during situations like this.

617
00:40:59,707 --> 00:41:00,833
[Arnaldo] We need to be discreet.

618
00:41:00,916 --> 00:41:03,586
We Ardientes can't let the people worry.

619
00:41:04,420 --> 00:41:07,673
What if I wasn't just grazed
by the bullet?

620
00:41:08,090 --> 00:41:09,508
What if it was worse?

621
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:11,844
Well, as you can see,

622
00:41:11,927 --> 00:41:14,430
we have all the medical equipment needed.

623
00:41:15,681 --> 00:41:20,019
You know, we can handle every
emergency you can think of.

624
00:41:20,728 --> 00:41:23,898
Dr. Hizon is a good doctor.
He's trustworthy.

625
00:41:25,399 --> 00:41:27,026
How are you feeling? Does it still hurt?

626
00:41:31,780 --> 00:41:32,781
Ivy?

627
00:41:34,658 --> 00:41:35,659
Ivy?

628
00:41:38,996 --> 00:41:40,206
[sighs]

629
00:41:43,876 --> 00:41:48,214
[tense music playing]

630
00:42:22,790 --> 00:42:26,669
[tense music continues playing]

631
00:42:54,196 --> 00:42:59,118
[instrumental theme music playing]

632
00:43:12,256 --> 00:43:14,633
Such a naughty boy, Mr. Mayor.

633
00:43:19,513 --> 00:43:23,475
[instrumental theme music playing]

634
00:43:29,607 --> 00:43:31,650
Does your girlfriend know about you?

635
00:43:37,448 --> 00:43:38,449
I'm sorry.

636
00:43:58,427 --> 00:43:59,428
Governor?

637
00:44:01,347 --> 00:44:02,723
Has my husband arrived?

638
00:44:03,474 --> 00:44:05,225
I don't know, Governor. I just got here.

639
00:44:06,185 --> 00:44:08,437
What happened to that man
who wanted to kill me?

640
00:44:08,604 --> 00:44:10,105
We made sure to deal with him.

641
00:44:11,815 --> 00:44:13,734
But it looks like
it's an isolated incident.

642
00:44:15,194 --> 00:44:16,195
Uh…

643
00:44:16,445 --> 00:44:19,281
The man didn't seem to be in his
right mind, so I got rid of him.

644
00:44:19,782 --> 00:44:21,116
I dispatched him nice and clean.

645
00:44:21,200 --> 00:44:22,201
Good job.

646
00:44:28,207 --> 00:44:29,208
Thank you.

647
00:44:32,836 --> 00:44:33,837
[Arnaldo] Mom.

648
00:44:37,633 --> 00:44:39,426
Did you contact your father?

649
00:44:39,843 --> 00:44:42,054
Not yet, but I'll call him again.

650
00:44:44,390 --> 00:44:45,516
How are you feeling?

651
00:44:48,686 --> 00:44:49,770
I'm fine!

652
00:44:50,396 --> 00:44:52,773
Don't you worry about me. I'm fine.

653
00:45:00,656 --> 00:45:03,367
[phone ringing]

654
00:45:04,576 --> 00:45:05,828
Hello, Arnaldo. What is it?

655
00:45:06,161 --> 00:45:06,995
[Arnaldo] Dad, where are you?

656
00:45:07,079 --> 00:45:09,081
We've been trying to call you,
but we can't reach you.

657
00:45:10,457 --> 00:45:11,500
The signal's pretty weak.

658
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:13,043
You need to come home.

659
00:45:13,127 --> 00:45:14,044
Something happened.

660
00:45:15,170 --> 00:45:15,921
All right.

661
00:45:20,175 --> 00:45:23,137
[crickets chirping]

662
00:45:23,804 --> 00:45:26,849
[somber piano music playing]

663
00:45:30,769 --> 00:45:33,313
[phone ringing]

664
00:45:33,772 --> 00:45:34,982
[line ringing]

665
00:45:35,065 --> 00:45:38,986
[phone ringing]

666
00:45:44,408 --> 00:45:49,163
[phone ringing]

667
00:45:56,295 --> 00:46:00,924
[phone ringing]

668
00:46:05,596 --> 00:46:08,265
[grunting]

669
00:46:09,850 --> 00:46:11,810
[sobs]

670
00:46:34,374 --> 00:46:37,085
[Natalie] Arnaldo, I'm talking to you!

671
00:46:38,378 --> 00:46:39,922
-Arnaldo!
-What?!

672
00:46:40,339 --> 00:46:41,882
Why did you leave me there?!

673
00:46:42,007 --> 00:46:44,676
-You left me there to die!
-Can you please relax, hmm?

674
00:46:45,010 --> 00:46:46,094
You were safe.

675
00:46:46,178 --> 00:46:47,429
The shooter left when you came.

676
00:46:47,513 --> 00:46:50,933
You still left me! Why did you go?!

677
00:46:52,184 --> 00:46:55,646
What do you expect me to do?
My mom was scared,

678
00:46:55,729 --> 00:46:58,190
Ivy was hit by a bullet,
it was an emergency!

679
00:46:58,398 --> 00:47:00,901
So, is Ivy more important than me?

680
00:47:00,984 --> 00:47:03,278
-No.
-Is that what you're saying?!

681
00:47:05,239 --> 00:47:07,366
I can't talk to you
while you're like this.

682
00:47:07,783 --> 00:47:10,702
Can you please relax,
go rest, or something?

683
00:47:10,786 --> 00:47:12,538
I'll have Madrigal bring you home.

684
00:47:12,704 --> 00:47:14,748
-No, we need to talk!
-Natalie.

685
00:47:15,791 --> 00:47:17,584
Listen. Please go home.

686
00:47:18,043 --> 00:47:19,044
Go on.

687
00:47:20,212 --> 00:47:21,463
Madrigal, bring her home.

688
00:47:21,964 --> 00:47:23,090
Arnaldo!

689
00:47:37,229 --> 00:47:39,773
[pensive music playing]

690
00:47:48,782 --> 00:47:52,035
Are you okay? You've been quiet all night.

691
00:47:53,537 --> 00:47:54,663
I'm fine.

692
00:47:56,123 --> 00:47:57,207
It'll pass.

693
00:47:57,874 --> 00:47:59,084
Did something happen?

694
00:48:02,337 --> 00:48:06,633
Nothing. Nanny, can I stay here tonight?

695
00:48:17,769 --> 00:48:19,104
You weren't supposed to hit anyone!

696
00:48:19,855 --> 00:48:21,523
I didn't expect her to block the shot.

697
00:48:24,401 --> 00:48:25,819
They think you're dead now.

698
00:48:26,361 --> 00:48:28,614
So leave this town and never come back!

699
00:48:30,282 --> 00:48:33,035
Go on. Go!

700
00:48:33,327 --> 00:48:37,372
[tense music playing]

701
00:48:47,633 --> 00:48:49,301
[Emilia] <i>I became a murderer</i>

702
00:48:49,384 --> 00:48:50,636
<i>because of my love for you!</i>

703
00:48:50,719 --> 00:48:53,347
<i>You didn't think how that affected Diego.</i>

704
00:48:53,430 --> 00:48:57,267
<i>You killed his best friend!</i>
<i>You wiped out an entire family!</i>

705
00:48:57,434 --> 00:48:59,311
[Jepoy] <i>Ivy, I know where</i>
<i>they buried your mother.</i>

706
00:48:59,394 --> 00:49:00,520
<i>Where are you? I'm going there!</i>

707
00:49:00,604 --> 00:49:03,231
<i>I don't care about</i>
<i>the Ardientes! Where are you?</i>

708
00:49:03,315 --> 00:49:05,817
[Emilia] <i>About Ivy… Be careful around her.</i>

709
00:49:05,901 --> 00:49:09,363
<i>I'm not sure if she's showing us</i>
<i>her true colors.</i>

710
00:49:09,446 --> 00:49:10,906
<i>The Ardientes are here.</i>

711
00:49:11,156 --> 00:49:13,950
[Ivy] <i>I want you to remember my face.</i>

712
00:49:14,785 --> 00:49:20,040
<i>I am Ivy Aguas, and I am vengeance.</i>
